{
  "answer": "The Grotesque Tree is a level-1 encounter threat in the garden site, tied to Hempholm and the conk. It\u2019s a Huge plant with natural armor 11 and 39 HP, so it\u2019s not a long-haul boss, but it can be nasty because it controls space at extreme range.\n\nIts real danger is battlefield control: Branch reaches 60 ft., hits for 1d4+3 slashing, and can trigger Snare on a failed DC 13 Dex or Str save to grapple and suspend a target 20 ft. up. It can hold two targets at once and then drag them closer on subsequent turns, or Sling a grappled creature 60 ft. for more bludgeoning damage and a DC 13 Dex save. That means the fight wants vertical threat, forced repositioning, and a way to punish isolated PCs.\n\nWeakness-wise, fire is the obvious lever: it has fire vulnerability, plus bludgeoning resistance and piercing immunity. Blind beyond 600 ft. is mostly irrelevant at this scale, but it does mean it\u2019s not a sensory omnivore.",
